# Backend process-environment reference; NOT an automatically loaded .env file.
# Settings reads os.getenv directly. Copying this file does not configure service.
# Prefer repository-root CLI: app/backend/.venv/bin/contextcore serve --data-dir ...
# CLI resolves the data directory and sets both variables in its own process.
# Without CLI/environment, config.py's direct-import database fallback is inside
# app/backend; it is not the CLI's macOS platform data-directory default.

# Optional for explicit non-CLI process setup; omit when not intentionally needed:
# CONTEXTCORE_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/isolated-contextcore-data
# CONTEXTCORE_DB=/absolute/path/to/isolated-contextcore-data/contextcore.db

# Hook subprocess only, not service/Vite configuration:
# CONTEXTCORE_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8420
# CONTEXTCORE_CREDENTIAL_PATH=/absolute/path/to/agent.token
# CONTEXTCORE_TOKEN is a direct hook-token override, intentionally not assigned
# here. Prefer a separately authorized generated 0600 credential file.

# Web sessions use opaque random IDs in an in-memory store, not signed cookies.
# CONTEXTCORE_SESSION_SECRET is not a cookie-signing setup option.
# CONTEXTCORE_RELEASE_ID is set/validated by release tooling; do not forge it.
# Never commit secrets, export real tokens into shell history, or assume dotenv
# autoloading. See ../../README.md and ../../../SECURITY.md for operational policy.
